// Syncthing ignore rules shared by every device that syncs this Solaris checkout.
// Each device's .stignore (never synced by Syncthing, gitignored here) holds any device-only rules
// first and `#include .stglobalignore` last: Syncthing applies the first rule that matches, so a
// device rule placed after the include loses to any shared rule here (a `!` exception there never
// takes effect). Edit this file, not the per-device copies. Syncthing treats a missing include file
// as an error, so a new device needs this file in place before its folder starts. Do not ignore
// .memory/ : that layer is how a session on one machine sees operating memory written on another.

(?d).DS_Store
(?d).Spotlight-V100
(?d).Trashes
(?d)Thumbs.db
(?d)desktop.ini

(?d)**/.venv
(?d)**/.venv*
(?d)**/node_modules
(?d)**/.npm

(?d)**/__pycache__
(?d)**/*.pyc
(?d)**/*.pyo
(?d)**/*.pyd
(?d)**/.pytest_cache
(?d)**/.ruff_cache
(?d)**/.mypy_cache
(?d)**/*.egg-info

(?d)/.tmp
(?d)/.tools

(?d)**/*.nosync
(?d)**/*.noSync
(?d)**/.playwright*
(?d)**/dist
(?d)**/build

// Solaris tools write a temp file and rename it over the target (solaris/tools/fileio.py).
(?d)**/.solaris-tmp-*

// Git runs only on the machine that holds a repo's clone; the other machines keep no .git. No (?d):
// a directory deleted on another device must not take that clone (and any unpushed commits) with it.
**/.git

// Project data and run outputs (the ai-pack's local-only `__data/` and `__out/`): large,
// regenerated, and kept on the machine that produced them. No (?d), for the same reason.
**/__data
**/__out

// Per-machine runtime (gitignored; tokens and local overrides). No (?d): deleting a copy here
// must not delete another machine's.
/.mcp.json
/.cursor/mcp.json
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/agents

// Conflict copies in memory folders stay on the machine that lost: the sweep (every session start
// and every prompt) merges each .jsonl copy there into its canonical log and reports any copy it
// leaves. These lines match the folders the sweep covers (_memory_roots in
// solaris/tools/read_first.py, plus each one's per-machine interactions/ log folder; keep them in
// step). A conflict copy anywhere else syncs like any other file, so every device sees the losing edit.
/.memory/*.sync-conflict-*
/.memory/interactions/*.sync-conflict-*
/projects/*/*/.memory/*.sync-conflict-*
/projects/*/*/.memory/interactions/*.sync-conflict-*
/projects/*/*/*/.memory/*.sync-conflict-*
/projects/*/*/*/.memory/interactions/*.sync-conflict-*
/projects/*/*/*/*/.memory/*.sync-conflict-*
/projects/*/*/*/*/.memory/interactions/*.sync-conflict-*
